' M-ROKU-06 (review roku__crossfe M6): design-plane law — the WHOLE channel is
' laid out on a hardcoded 1280x720 plane (112 XML width/height/loadWidth/
' loadHeight attribute pins across 37 files at cce1b34; PlayerScene.brs sizes
' the Video node
' 1280x720 at :1185 and :3000; there is zero coordinate scaling anywhere —
' no resolutionRatio, viewBounds, GetVisibleRect or root Group scale, and
' videoMode is read only for the About screen). With 'full' declared beside
' 'hd', RokuOS runs 1080p devices NATIVELY at 1920x1080 and the 720p layout
' sits unscaled in the top-left two-thirds of the screen. Declaring 'hd'
' alone makes the OS render the 1280x720 canvas and upscale it — the standard
' fixed-layout posture. 'sd' is intentionally absent: the app is https-only
' modern and a 1280-wide plane never fits a 640x480 screen. Re-declare 'full'
' only TOGETHER with a real resolution-aware layout; CHECK38 pins the
' declaration, the plane's FHD-only outliers and this comment's presence.
ui_resolutions=hd

' M-ROKU-07 (review roku__crossfe M7): rsg_version selects the SceneGraph
' OBSERVER CALLBACK MODEL, not a component-library release — its documented
' value space is 1.0/1.1/1.2/1.3 (developer.roku.com/dev/docs/channel-manifest,
' retrieved 2026-10-29; the entry defaults to 1.2 as of Roku OS 9.3). The
' long-shipped 7.0 was RSG's package version bled into the wrong key: devices
' silently IGNORE unknown values, so the line was a false-comfort knob brighterscript
' cannot flag (it treats unknown-but-semver values as valid by design).
' The same page: "You must set this parameter to rsg_version=1.3 by
' October 1, 2026, to continue passing certification testing" — that deadline
' has passed and this channel carries a live certification intent
' (docs/certification.md), so 1.3 is the cert-required shipped value.
' Feature-usage honesty: the channel relies on NO >=1.1-exclusive behavior —
' the 489 ObserveField sites and roSGNodeEvent task loops are core SceneGraph
' at every rsg version — and 1.3 costs nothing: its hard rule is that Eval()
' cannot be used at rsg_version>=1.2, and the shipped .brs set calls Eval zero
' times. CHECK39 pins the value space, the 1.3 certification posture, this
' comment's presence and the Eval() extinction.
rsg_version=1.3

screensaver_title=Phlix
